AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:bf") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:dph") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0201090910") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0716720094") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0879010479") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Wikipedia:Glycolysis") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0006096> "The chemical reactions and pathways resulting in the breakdown of a carbohydrate into pyruvate, with the concomitant production of a small amount of ATP and the reduction of NAD(P) to NAD(P)H. Glycolysis begins with the metabolism of a carbohydrate to generate products that can enter the pathway and ends with the production of pyruvate. Pyruvate may be converted to acetyl-coenzyme A, ethanol, lactate, or other small molecules.")
