# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0014835> (myoblast differentiation involved in skeletal muscle regeneration)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "CL:0000056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:ef") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:mtg_muscle") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16607119") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0014835> "The process in which a relatively unspecialized satellite cell acquires specialized features of a myoblast. This occurs as part of skeletal muscle regeneration. A myoblast is a mononucleate cell type that, by fusion with other myoblasts, gives rise to the myotubes that eventually develop into skeletal muscle fibers.")
