# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0015399> (primary active transmembrane transporter activity)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:mtg_transport") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31613498") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0015399> "Enables the transfer of a solute from one side of a membrane to the other, up the solute's concentration gradient, by binding the solute and undergoing a series of conformational changes. Transport works equally well in either direction and is powered by a primary energy source. Primary energy sources known to be coupled to transport are chemical such as ATP hydrolysis, redox energy and photon energy.")
