# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0030098> (lymphocyte differentiation)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "CL:0000542") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:curators") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0030098> "The process in which a relatively unspecialized precursor cell acquires specialized features of a lymphocyte. A lymphocyte is a leukocyte commonly found in the blood and lymph that has the characteristics of a large nucleus, a neutral staining cytoplasm, and prominent heterochromatin.")
