AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0030217> "Note that the term 'thymocyte differentiation' was merged into this term because thymocytes are T cells, and thus the term was essentially redundant. Note that immunologists typically use the word 'development' to refer to cells of B or T cell lineages undergoing the process that GO describes as 'cell differentiation'.")
