# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0031049> (programmed DNA elimination)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:mah") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:ns") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18708581") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24886889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32986476") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0031049> "A process in which genomic fragments or entire chromosomes are eliminated from somatic cells or from micronuclei of ciliates. This process occurs in the developing macronucleus (anlage) of a ciliate, as well as in other species, including vertebrates and is an irreversible mechanism of gene silencing.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000233> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0031049> "https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/22815"^^xsd:anyURI)
